1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,544
OKAY, PICK A CARD.
OKAY.

2
00:00:02,544 --> 00:00:05,673
ALL RIGHT.
NOW... MEMORIZE IT.

3
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:07,048
YOU GOT IT?
OH, YES.

4
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:10,803
OKAY. IS THAT YOUR CARD?

5
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:17,476
YES.
( chuckling ):
YEAH, IT IS.

6
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:18,602
HEY, GUYS.

7
00:00:18,602 --> 00:00:20,855
HI, THERE!
Ben: HI!

8
00:00:20,855 --> 00:00:22,898
GUESS WHAT?

9
00:00:22,898 --> 00:00:25,651
BEN IS GOING TO BE
IN A TV COMMERCIAL.

10
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,611
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

11
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:28,779
WELL... IT'S NOT FOR SURE

12
00:00:28,779 --> 00:00:30,614
BUT, UH, WE MET THIS GUY
IN THE PARK

13
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:32,616
WHO THOUGHT BEN
WAS REALLY CUTE, YOU KNOW...

14
00:00:32,616 --> 00:00:34,034
WHICH HE IS.

15
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:36,161
UM, ANYWHO, HE, UH,
HE GAVE US HIS CARD

16
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,788
AND TOLD US
TO BRING HIM DOWN

17
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:39,832
FOR THIS COMMERCIAL
HE'S AUDITIONING.

18
00:00:39,832 --> 00:00:42,543
WHOA. THIS GUY'S, LIKE

19
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:44,461
THE BIGGEST COMMERCIAL-CASTING
DIRECTOR IN TOWN!

20
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,088
BEN TAKES ONE LOUSY WALK
IN THE PARK

21
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,590
AND GETS AN AUDITION?!

22
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:53,929
I MEAN, "WAY TO GO, BEN!"

23
00:00:55,806 --> 00:00:58,183
MAN, I'VE BEEN IN THAT PARK
A MILLION TIMES.

24
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:00,185
NO ONE'S EVER OFFERED ME
AN AUDITION.

25
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,980
I KNOW. IT'S CRAZY--
WE WERE JUST PUSHING
BEN ON THE SWINGS...

26
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:06,692
I'M ALWAYS ON THE SWINGS!

27
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:09,069
( whining ):
WHAT AM I DOING WRONG?

28
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,111
THAT.

29
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:22,499
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

30
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:24,752
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

31
00:01:24,752 --> 00:01:27,462
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

32
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:31,174
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

33
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:34,553
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

34
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:37,222
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

35
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:41,100
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

36
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,311
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

37
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:45,981
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

38
00:01:45,981 --> 00:01:47,399
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

39
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:51,110
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

40
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:56,075
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

41
00:02:01,914 --> 00:02:04,332
OKAY, GOT TO GO. WISH ME LUCK.

42
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:06,167
HEY, RACH, NOW THAT YOU'RE
WORKING AT RALPH LAUREN

43
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:08,336
CAN YOU BRING ME BACK
SOME OF THOSE POLO SHIRTS?

44
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:09,838
UH, WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

45
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:11,172
I DON'T KNOW
IF I'D FEEL COMFORTABLE

46
00:02:11,172 --> 00:02:13,717
STEALING ON MY VERY FIRST DAY.

47
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:16,971
UNWILLING TO STEAL FROM WORK...

48
00:02:16,971 --> 00:02:18,806
INTERESTING.

49
00:02:18,806 --> 00:02:20,140
BESIDES, IF
ANYBODY'S GOING
TO GET FREE STUFF

50
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,224
IT'S GOING TO BE ME.

51
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,726
OKAY, GUYS,
WAY TO WISH ME LUCK.

52
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:24,436
GOOD LUCK.
HAVE A GOOD DAY.

53
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:25,854
BYE.

54
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:28,690
OKAY, LET'S DISCUSS
RACHEL'S BIRTHDAY.

55
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:31,234
I SAY WE THROW HER
A SURPRISE PARTY THIS WEEKEND.

56
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:33,737
WHOA, BUT HER BIRTHDAY'S
NOT FOR, LIKE, ANOTHER MONTH.

57
00:02:33,737 --> 00:02:36,031
OKAY, BUT IF WE THROW HER
A PARTY ON HER BIRTHDAY

58
00:02:36,031 --> 00:02:38,867
THEN IT'S NOT A SURPRISE.

59
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,953
I THINK THAT'S A GREAT IDEA.
WE CAN HAVE A DINNER PARTY

60
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:42,663
AND JUST INVITE
HER CLOSE FRIENDS.

61
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,790
ROSS! WE'RE HAVING
A SURPRISE PARTY FOR RACHEL!

62
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:45,958
Ross:
OKAY!

63
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:47,751
DONE.

64
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:51,463
OKAY, GREAT, SO DO YOU WANT
TO DO IT TOGETHER?

65
00:02:51,463 --> 00:02:53,507
I WOULD LOVE 
TO DO IT TOGETHER.
OOH!

66
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:57,636
( fiendish laughter )

67
00:02:57,636 --> 00:02:59,721
THEY'RE GOING TO DO IT
TOGETHER.

68
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,598
DUDE, THAT'S MY GIRLFRIEND.

69
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:05,477
OH, SO I GOT
TO SHUT IT DOWN NOW?

70
00:03:05,477 --> 00:03:07,521
ALL RIGHT. I
GOT TO TAKE OFF.

71
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:09,188
I'M PICKING UP BEN
AND THEN WE'RE OFF

72
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:11,066
TO THE BIG AUDITION.

73
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:12,442
I BET IT'S GOING
TO BE WEIRD SEEING SOME ACTOR

74
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,486
PRETENDING TO
BE BEN'S DAD.
YEAH.

75
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:18,406
WEIRDER THAN SEEING
HIS TWO MOMS MAKE OUT?

76
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:19,950
WHOA, WHOA, "DAD"?

77
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:21,326
THERE'S A DAD IN THE COMMERCIAL?

78
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:23,162
YEAH. THE DAD AND BEN EAT SOUP

79
00:03:23,162 --> 00:03:24,913
AND PRETEND TO ENJOY IT.

80
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,414
MAYBE I'LL GO DOWN WITH YOU

81
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:28,167
AND SEE IF I CAN GET
AN AUDITION AS THE DAD.

82
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:30,502
WHO BETTER THAN TO PLAY
BEN'S FATHER THAN HIS GODFATHER?

83
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:31,795
YOU'RE NOT HIS GODFATHER.

84
00:03:31,795 --> 00:03:34,506
WHAT?!

85
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:37,801
ARE YOU KIDDING?!

86
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:39,094
OF COURSE I AM.

87
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:40,387
( sighing )

88
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:42,597
OKAY, LET'S GO,
GODFATHER.

89
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,058
ALL RIGHT! WHOA.

90
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:51,606
HEY! I'M IN.

91
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:53,441
THEY'RE GOING TO
LET ME AUDITION.

92
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:55,110
REALLY? THAT'S GREAT.

93
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:57,320
IT TURNS OUT ONE OF
THE CASTING LADIES

94
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,114
HAS ACTUALLY
SEEN ME IN A PLAY

95
00:03:59,114 --> 00:04:02,076
SO I STEERED
CLEAR OF HER.

96
00:04:02,076 --> 00:04:03,869
Carol:
HEY, THAT KID
LOOKS FAMILIAR.

97
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,871
OH, YEAH, YEAH.
HE'S DONE TONS
OF COMMERCIALS.

98
00:04:05,871 --> 00:04:08,540
I'VE SEEN HIM IN, LIKE,
SUGAR SMACKS, PLAYSTATION

99
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,042
AND THAT ONE FOR
THE PHONE COMPANY.

100
00:04:10,042 --> 00:04:11,668
IN FACT, HE WAS
SO GOOD IN THAT ONE

101
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:14,963
HE ACTUALLY CONVINCED ME
TO SWITCH PHONE COMPANIES.

102
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,758
( chuckling ):
CHANDLER WAS MAD...

103
00:04:17,758 --> 00:04:19,634
YEAH, WELL, HE'S NOT GOING
TO GET THIS ONE, ALL RIGHT?

104
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:21,302
BEN IS WAY CUTER
THAN THAT KID.

105
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:23,263
I MEAN, LOOK AT HIM--
LOOK AT YOU!

106
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:26,558
( speaking gibberish )

107
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:29,310
( sniffling )

108
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,729
( chuckling ):
THAT'S... GREAT.

109
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,773
LISTEN, WOULDN'T IT
BE GREAT, THOUGH

110
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:34,315
IF I GOT TO PLAY
BEN'S DAD?

111
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:37,402
JOEY, YOU LOOK
NOTHING LIKE BEN.

112
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,196
I LOOK MORE LIKE
HIM THAN YOU DO.

113
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:42,991
YOU KNOW, I REALLY DON'T
KNOW YOU WELL ENOUGH

114
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,284
FOR YOU TO DO THAT.

115
00:04:50,124 --> 00:04:52,000
SO, IT'S DOWN
TO THESE TWO.

116
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,587
NANCY, I KNOW
YOU LIKE THIS ONE,
AND I THINK I AGREE.

117
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:57,131
RACHEL, WHAT DO
YOU THINK?

118
00:04:57,131 --> 00:04:59,299
WELL, UM, I MEAN,
THAT ONE IS PRETTY

119
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,927
BUT, OH, I JUST...
I JUST LOVE THIS FABRIC.

120
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:03,553
SORRY.

121
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:04,972
OH, DON'T BE SORRY.

122
00:05:04,972 --> 00:05:06,598
IT'S PART OF YOUR JOB
TO GIVE YOUR OPINIONS

123
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:09,559
AND THEN I TAKE CREDIT
FOR THEM. I'M KIDDING.

124
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:11,061
SHE IS KIDDING...

125
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:13,147
BUT DON'T EVER DISAGREE
WITH HER AGAIN.

126
00:05:13,147 --> 00:05:14,856
OKAY, NOW I'M KIDDING.

127
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:18,235
( nervous laugh ):
OH, WHAT A FUN OFFICE.

128
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:21,113
I DON'T KNOW WHICH ONE,
BUT I DO KNOW I NEED A CIGARETTE

129
00:05:21,113 --> 00:05:23,657
SO WHAT DO YOU SAY
WE TAKE A BREAK, WE GO OUTSIDE

130
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:26,201
AND WE'LL FIGURE THIS THING OUT
WHEN WE COME BACK?

131
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:29,830
RACHEL?

132
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:30,831
YEAH?

133
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:31,915
YOU SMOKE?

134
00:05:31,915 --> 00:05:33,374
OH, NO. MY DAD'S A DOCTOR

135
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:35,877
AND HE WOULD ALWAYS TELL ME
JUST HORROR STORIES...

136
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:42,341
ABOUT, UH, GHOSTS
AND GOBLINS...

137
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:47,139
WHO... TOTALLY SUPPORTED
THE PRINCESS'S RIGHT TO SMOKE.

138
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:54,938
AND THEN THEY CAME BACK
FROM SMOKING

139
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:57,356
AND THEY HAD MADE ALL
OF THE DECISIONS WITHOUT ME.

140
00:05:57,356 --> 00:05:59,151
THAT DOESN'T SEEM FAIR.

141
00:05:59,151 --> 00:06:00,735
I KNOW.
IT'S LIKE I'M BEING PUNISHED

142
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,946
FOR NOT HAVING THIS DISGUSTING,
POISONOUS HABIT.

143
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:04,906
YEAH, IT IS THE BEST.

144
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:07,868
I MEAN, WHAT IF THIS KEEPS
HAPPENING, YOU KNOW?

145
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:09,661
THEY'LL-THEY'LL
BE OUTSIDE SMOKING

146
00:06:09,661 --> 00:06:12,289
MAKING ALL THE DECISIONS,
AND I'LL JUST BE UP IN MY OFFICE

147
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:16,084
BREATHING IN
MY STUPID CLEAN AIR, YOU KNOW?

148
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:18,128
AND THEN WHEN THE DAY COMES WHEN
KIM WANTS TO PROMOTE ONE OF US

149
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:19,213
WHO DO YOU THINK
SHE'S GOING TO PICK--

150
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:22,257
ME OR SMOKEY SMOKERSON?

151
00:06:22,257 --> 00:06:24,092
RACHEL, YOU CAN GO DOWN THERE.
YOU DON'T HAVE TO SMOKE.

152
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:26,928
JUST SAY YOU WANT TO
GET SOME... FRESH AIR.

153
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:30,098
YEAH, I COULD DO THAT.

154
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:33,268
YEAH, OR YOU COULD JUST DO
THE EASY THING AND SMOKE.

155
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:34,644
( knocking )
HEY.

156
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,437
RACH, DO YOU WANT
TO GO GET COFFEE?

157
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:37,480
OH, I WOULD LOVE TO.

158
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,481
OH, GOOD!

159
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:39,983
I'LL GO TOO, BABE.

160
00:06:39,983 --> 00:06:41,735
OH, GOOD.

161
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:42,986
YAY.
YAY.
YAH.

162
00:06:42,986 --> 00:06:44,445
OH, I CHANGED MY MIND.

163
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:46,948
OKAY.

164
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:49,159
OKAY, LET'S TALK
ABOUT THE PARTY.

165
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:51,119
I HAVE SO MANY IDEAS.

166
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,204
ME, TOO!

167
00:06:52,204 --> 00:06:54,413
OH!

168
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:55,665
YEAH!
OH, LOOK AT THAT.

169
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,501
ALL RIGHT.

170
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,212
HERE'S A LITTLE
SKETCH OF THE CAKE.

171
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,880
UH-HUH.
SEE?

172
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,382
UM, SOME SAMPLE MENUS, UM...

173
00:07:03,382 --> 00:07:04,758
YOU KNOW, I THOUGHT
WE'D START OUT

174
00:07:04,758 --> 00:07:07,386
WITH TUSCAN-STYLE
FINGER FOOD, OKAY?

175
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:10,180
AND FOR MUSIC, HERE'S
AN ALPHABETIZED LIST
OF ALL OF MY CDs.

176
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,765
I'VE HIGHLIGHTED THE ONES

177
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:14,393
THAT'LL GO REALLY
GOOD WITH THE FOOD.

178
00:07:14,393 --> 00:07:16,353
WHAT HAPPENED
TO THE INTIMATE DINNER PARTY?

179
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:18,479
YOU KNOW, WE'RE NOT
DOING THAT, OKAY?

180
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:20,107
WOW. ALL RIGHT.

181
00:07:20,107 --> 00:07:22,650
LOOKS LIKE YOU TOOK CARE
OF EVERYTHING.

182
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,069
THANKS A LOT,
CO-HOST.

183
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:25,320
WAIT A MINUTE.

184
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,863
I DIDN'T TAKE CARE
OF EVERYTHING.

185
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,740
THERE'S PLENTY OF THINGS
FOR YOU TO DO.

186
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,075
UH-HUH. LIKE WHAT?

187
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:32,119
CUPS!

188
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:35,080
CUPS? YOU'RE
GIVING ME CUPS?

189
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,873
AND ICE.

190
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:39,376
CUPS AND ICE?

191
00:07:39,376 --> 00:07:41,628
OH, I GET TO BE IN
CHARGE OF CUPS AND ICE?

192
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:44,423
ALL RIGHT, FINE.

193
00:07:44,423 --> 00:07:47,050
OKAY, I WILL BE IN
CHARGE OF CUPS AND ICE.

194
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,509
WAIT A MINUTE,
I CAN GET ICE
AT THE RESTAURANT.

195
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:49,469
I GOT IT! MINE!

196
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,556
Monica:
HEY.
HI.

197
00:07:53,556 --> 00:07:54,682
HOW'D THE AUDITION GO?

198
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:57,394
NOT SO GOOD.

199
00:07:57,394 --> 00:07:58,853
NOW, WAIT A MINUTE.

200
00:07:58,853 --> 00:08:00,605
ARE YOU DOING JOEY'S...

201
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:03,275
"THE AUDITION DIDN'T
GO SO WELL...

202
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:04,901
YEAH, IT DID!"

203
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:07,821
YEAH, I AM!

204
00:08:07,821 --> 00:08:10,407
( screaming )

205
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:11,866
YEAH, BEN GOT
A SECOND AUDITION!

206
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:13,034
GREAT!

207
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:15,287
YEAH, I HAD TO TEACH
ROSS MY BIT

208
00:08:15,287 --> 00:08:18,165
'CAUSE I ACTUALLY DIDN'T
GET A CALLBACK.

209
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:21,168
YOU GOT A CALLBACK,
TOO, DIDN'T YOU?

210
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:24,754
YEAH, I DID!

211
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:32,346
HEY, RACHEL, WHAT ARE
YOU DOING OUT HERE?

212
00:08:32,346 --> 00:08:35,056
WELL, YOU KNOW, IT GOT
KIND OF LONELY UP THERE

213
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:37,267
SO I JUST THOUGHT
I WOULD COME OUT HERE AND...

214
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:40,103
GET SOME FRESH AIR.
( coughing )

215
00:08:40,103 --> 00:08:42,105
NANCY AND I WERE
TALKING ABOUT THE
FALL COLLECTION.

216
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:43,315
OH, GREAT.

217
00:08:43,315 --> 00:08:45,192
SO, ANYWAY...
( coughing )

218
00:08:45,192 --> 00:08:46,776
HONEY, I'M SORRY.
WE'RE SMOKING
ALL OVER YOU.

219
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,111
OH, THAT'S OKAY.

220
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:49,821
WE'LL MOVE. YOU
STAY RIGHT HERE.

221
00:08:49,821 --> 00:08:51,823
Nancy:
SO I WAS
THINKING...

222
00:08:51,823 --> 00:08:53,158
THANKS.

223
00:08:53,158 --> 00:08:54,617
OH, THAT'S
GREAT.

224
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,411
YOU ARE THE BEST.

225
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:59,747
EXCUSE ME, CAN I
BUM ONE OF THOSE?

226
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,124
YEAH, YOU KNOW, ACTUALLY...

227
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,502
( both laughing )

228
00:09:03,502 --> 00:09:06,629
OKAY, OKAY, WHAT'S
SO FUNNY OVER HERE?

229
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:08,923
I THOUGHT YOU
DIDN'T SMOKE.

230
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:10,633
OH, YOU KNOW, I-I THOUGHT

231
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:15,138
YOU GUYS MEANT
MARIJUANA CIGARETTES, YOU KNOW?

232
00:09:15,138 --> 00:09:16,931
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?
LIKE, DOOBIES?

233
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:21,520
ACTUALLY, I THOUGHT TO MYSELF,
"WOW, THOSE GUYS ARE CRAZY!"

234
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,480
BUT, NO, ACTUALLY,
I SMOKE THE REGULAR ONES

235
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,690
ALL... ALL THE TIME.

236
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:26,941
WE GET HIGH.

237
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,405
( stammering ):
ME, TOO.

238
00:09:32,531 --> 00:09:34,491
I'M KIDDING.
OH!

239
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:36,076
( weakly ):
ME, TOO.

240
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:41,206
OH, GOD, THIS IS
SO NERVE-RACKING.

241
00:09:41,206 --> 00:09:42,999
HOW-HOW DO YOU DO THIS?

242
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:46,878
WELL, FORTUNATELY, I DON'T
GET MANY CALLBACKS, SO...

243
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:48,213
IS IT A GOOD SIGN
THAT THEY ASKED US 

244
00:09:48,213 --> 00:09:49,756
TO HANG AROUND
AFTER THE AUDITION?

245
00:09:49,756 --> 00:09:50,965
WHO KNOWS?

246
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:57,305
OKAY, UH, WE HAVE NARROWED IT
DOWN TO RAYMOND, BEN

247
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,266
KYLE AND JOEY.

248
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:01,226
THE REST OF YOU,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

249
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:03,853
YES! I KNEW IT!

250
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,397
( sighing ):
BYE-BYE...

251
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:09,692
SO LONG...

252
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:11,361
LATER.

253
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:14,573
ROSS, THIS IS GREAT.

254
00:10:14,573 --> 00:10:15,865
I MIGHT ACTUALLY GET
TO PLAY BEN'S DAD.

255
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:16,950
YEAH!

256
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:18,368
ACTUALLY, THAT
CAN'T HAPPEN.

257
00:10:18,368 --> 00:10:20,287
BECAUSE YOU ALL HAVE
SUCH DIFFERENT LOOKS

258
00:10:20,287 --> 00:10:21,829
WE'RE PUTTING YOU
WITH RAYMOND

259
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:23,748
AND KYLE WITH BEN.

260
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:27,961
SO IT'LL EITHER BE
YOU TWO OR YOU TWO.

261
00:10:27,961 --> 00:10:30,380
OH, MAN...

262
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,257
THIS IS GOING TO BE
KIND OF WEIRD.

263
00:10:32,257 --> 00:10:33,550
YEAH, IT IS..

264
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:36,136
YEAH. IT'S GOING
TO BE WEIRD.

265
00:10:38,096 --> 00:10:40,014
NO, WE'RE-WE'RE,
LIKE, BEST FRIENDS.

266
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:42,058
THAT'S-THAT'S
WHY IT'S WEIRD.

267
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,393
OH, OH.

268
00:10:43,393 --> 00:10:46,854
I-I THOUGHT WE WERE
JUST... TALKING.

269
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:54,237
HEY.

270
00:10:54,237 --> 00:10:56,323
IS IT OKAY IF I LEAVE
THIS STUFF HERE

271
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:58,032
TILL RACHEL'S
BIRTHDAY PARTY?

272
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,326
SURE. WHAT'S
IN THEM?

273
00:10:59,326 --> 00:11:01,369
UM, CUPS.

274
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:04,623
OH, GOOD, BECAUSE WE GOT RACHEL
800 GALLONS OF WATER.

275
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,001
SERIOUSLY, THAT'S
A LOT OF CUPS.

276
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:10,462
YEAH, WELL, THAT'S 'CAUSE
I'M IN CHARGE OF CUPS AND ICE

277
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:12,046
AND MONICA IS GOING
TO RUE THE DAY

278
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:13,965
THAT SHE PUT ME IN CHARGE
OF CUPS AND ICE.

279
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:17,844
YOU KNOW, I RUED THE DAY ONCE.

280
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:19,262
DIDN'T GET
A WHOLE LOT ELSE DONE.

281
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:23,391
OKAY, TIME TO BRING UP
THE REST OF THE CUPS.

282
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,561
OH, HEY, JOEY.

283
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:27,562
HEY, PHEEBS.

284
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:29,105
Ross:
HEY.

285
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:31,858
ROSS, GOOD.
I'M, UH, GLAD YOU'RE HERE.

286
00:11:31,858 --> 00:11:33,568
I WANT TO TALK TO YOU
ABOUT SOMETHING.

287
00:11:33,568 --> 00:11:35,487
OH? WHAT'S UP?

288
00:11:35,487 --> 00:11:38,365
WELL, I'VE BEEN THINKING ABOUT
THIS WHOLE COMMERCIAL THING.

289
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:40,241
YOU KNOW,
ME GOING UP AGAINST BEN

290
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,243
THE TWO OF US COMPETING, AND...

291
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:44,329
WELL, THAT CAN'T LEAD
TO ANYTHING GOOD

292
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:47,706
SO... I THINK
I'M JUST GOING TO STEP ASIDE.

293
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:50,960
I'M GOING TO TELL THEM
THAT I WON'T AUDITION.

294
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:54,005
WOW, UH...
JOEY, THAT'S... THAT'S GREAT.

295
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:55,465
THANKS, MAN.

296
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,013
THAT'S IT?

297
00:12:03,764 --> 00:12:05,183
YOU-YOU'RE GOING
TO LET ME DO THIS?

298
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:07,060
THIS IS MY CAREER
WE'RE TALKING ABOUT HERE.

299
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,562
BUT... BUT YOU JUST...

300
00:12:08,562 --> 00:12:12,106
I JUST SAID THAT SO YOU WOULDN'T
LET BEN DO IT.

301
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:14,859
LOOK, ROSS, IF ANYONE SHOULD
STEP ASIDE, IT SHOULD BE BEN.

302
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:17,195
WHAT?
CHANDLER, TELL HIM.

303
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:22,158
WELL, LET ME... LET
ME GET THE DOOR FIRST.

304
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:25,495
OH, HI, NO ONE.

305
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:30,917
WHY SHOULD BEN
STEP ASIDE?

306
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:33,253
IT WAS HIS AUDITION
IN THE FIRST PLACE.

307
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:34,713
YOU JUST TAGGED ALONG.

308
00:12:34,713 --> 00:12:37,340
YOU'RE LIKE THE...
THE TAG-ALONG DAD.

309
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:39,217
AT LEAST I CARE
ABOUT HIS FEELINGS.

310
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:40,759
WH-WH-WHAT?

311
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:42,470
DO YOU KNOW HOW HARD
THIS WILL BE ON HIM

312
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:43,804
WHEN HE DOESN'T GET IT?

313
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:46,182
AND WHY WOULDN'T HE GET IT?

314
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:48,518
OH, COME ON.

315
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:49,686
HAVE YOU SEEN
WHAT MY KID CAN DO?

316
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:51,979
HUH?

317
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:53,607
I MEAN, HE DIALS PHONES

318
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:55,567
HE-HE EATS TORTILLA CHIPS.

319
00:12:55,567 --> 00:12:58,486
HE-HE PLAYS SOCCER WITH
THE CARTOON TIGER.

320
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:02,323
ARE YOU SAYING YOUR KID
EATS SOUP BETTER THAN MY KID?

321
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:05,285
YOU JUST GIVE HIM
A SPOON, BABY.

322
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:06,327
OH, YEAH? I GUESS WE'LL SEE.

323
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:07,954
YEAH

324
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:09,997
BECAUSE THIS COMMERCIAL
BELONGS TO ME AND MITCH.

325
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,666
YOUR KID'S NAME IS RAYMOND.

326
00:13:11,666 --> 00:13:12,791
YEAH, SO'S YOURS!

327
00:13:18,757 --> 00:13:21,342
HOW DID WORK GO?
OH, IT WAS GREAT.

328
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:24,387
I WENT DOWN THERE JUST
LIKE YOU SAID, YOU KNOW,
AND WE TALKED BUSINESS

329
00:13:24,387 --> 00:13:26,139
AND KIM TOTALLY TOOK
MY OPINIONS.

330
00:13:26,139 --> 00:13:27,848
YOU STINK.

331
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:30,435
THANKS.

332
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:32,186
NO, I'M-I'M SERIOUS.

333
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:33,772
WELL, THAT-THAT'S JUST
'CAUSE I WENT DOWN THERE

334
00:13:33,772 --> 00:13:35,148
AND THEY WERE ALL SMOKING.

335
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:37,942
THIS IS ACTUALLY THE
SMELL OF SUCCESS.

336
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:40,361
OKAY, BUT THERE'S
SOMETHING DIFFERENT, THOUGH.

337
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:42,280
OH, MY GOD. YOU SMOKED.

338
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,281
( gasping )

339
00:13:43,281 --> 00:13:44,741
I DID NOT.

340
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:48,244
YES, YOU DID. YOU LOOK HAPPY
AND SICK-- YOU SMOKED!

341
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:50,371
ALL RIGHT, FINE, BUT I HAD TO.

342
00:13:50,371 --> 00:13:52,499
I HAD TO DO IT FOR MY CAREER.

343
00:13:52,499 --> 00:13:56,503
I WISH I HAD TO SMOKE
FOR MY CAREER.

344
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:58,421
BUT IT'S SO GROSS.

345
00:13:58,421 --> 00:14:00,839
DON'T... NO, WELL, NO,
IT'S NOT THAT BAD, YOU KNOW.

346
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:03,343
IT'S... I MEAN, YEAH,
MY TONGUE FEELS A LITTLE FUZZY

347
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:05,345
AND MY FINGERS SORT OF SMELL.

348
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:08,889
I ACTUALLY FEEL
LIKE I COULD THROW UP.

349
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:10,975
OKAY, BUT YOU GOT
TO PUSH PAST THIS, OKAY?

350
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:14,020
BECAUSE IT'S ABOUT
TO GET SO GOOD.

351
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,062
CHANDLER.

352
00:14:16,523 --> 00:14:18,525
OH, I GOT TO TELL YOU,
YOU SMELL SO SMOKY

353
00:14:18,525 --> 00:14:19,734
I GOT... I-I GOT TO GET UP.

354
00:14:19,734 --> 00:14:21,736
WHAT?
I'M NOT KIDDING.

355
00:14:21,736 --> 00:14:24,030
I THINK YOU SMELL GREAT.

356
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:32,539
SO, WE'RE DECIDED--
NO ON PLAID, YES ON PINK.

357
00:14:32,539 --> 00:14:33,956
ABSOLUTELY.

358
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:36,209
I'M SO ON-BOARD.

359
00:14:36,209 --> 00:14:38,919
MM-HMM.

360
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:41,172
RACHEL, DIDN'T YOU
JUST LIGHT THAT?

361
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:42,923
YEAH, BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

362
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:46,010
I'M JUST REALLY, REALLY
TRYING TO CUT BACK, YOU KNOW.

363
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,637
GOOD LUCK, RACH.

364
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:52,183
I'VE ACTUALLY BEEN
THINKING ABOUT
QUITTING LATELY.

365
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:53,643
OH, WELL, SURE--
EVERY SUNDAY NIGHT

366
00:14:53,643 --> 00:14:54,977
I TELL MYSELF I'M QUITTING.

367
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:57,063
EVERY MONDAY MORNING,
IT'S LIKE...

368
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:58,105
TELL ME ABOUT IT.

369
00:14:58,105 --> 00:14:59,440
WELL, LET'S JUST QUIT.

370
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,401
WE'LL JUST QUIT.
LET'S ALL QUIT.

371
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:02,943
IT DOES SOUND APPEALING.

372
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:04,153
I NEVER COULD DO IT.

373
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,864
OH, BUT YOU COULD.
YOU CAN. ABSOLUTELY.

374
00:15:05,864 --> 00:15:07,532
WE CAN HELP
EACH OTHER OUT.

375
00:15:07,532 --> 00:15:08,991
YOU KNOW, WE COULD GET--
WHAT? WHAT?-- THOSE PATCHES.

376
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:11,703
WE COULD BE LIKE
THE PATCH SISTERS.

377
00:15:11,703 --> 00:15:13,496
WELL, YOU KNOW,
WE REALLY SHOULD QUIT.

378
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:14,831
OKAY, LET'S QUIT.

379
00:15:14,831 --> 00:15:17,124
YES. GREAT.
GIVE ME THOSE CIGS.

380
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:18,668
COME ON, GIVE IT. GIVE IT.

381
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:19,919
OUT, DONE. QUIT. WHOO!

382
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,131
MY LATE HUSBAND
GAVE ME THAT LIGHTER.

383
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:26,175
SHE'S FUNNY.

384
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,344
I'M NOT KIDDING.

385
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,555
OKAY, THEN. OKAY.

386
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,894
MMM... SOUP.

387
00:15:35,894 --> 00:15:38,479
MMM, SOUP.

388
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:42,275
MMM... SOUP.

389
00:15:42,275 --> 00:15:44,360
JOEY, ROSS IS GOING
TO BE HERE ANY SECOND.

390
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:47,154
WOULD YOU MIND WATCHING
BEN FOR ME WHILE I USE
THE LADIES ROOM?

391
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:48,448
OH, YEAH. NO PROBLEM.

392
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:51,785
MMM, SOUP.

393
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:01,377
HI, BEN.

394
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:02,962
SO YOU WANT TO BE
AN ACTOR, HUH?

395
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:05,757
WELL, I GOT TO TELL
YOU, IT'S NO PICNIC.

396
00:16:05,757 --> 00:16:06,966
THERE'S TONS OF REJECTION.

397
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:09,302
NO STABILITY.

398
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:13,347
I MEAN, ONE DAY YOU'RE
DR. DRAKE RAMORAY.

399
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:14,724
THE NEXT DAY,
YOU'RE EATING KETCHUP

400
00:16:14,724 --> 00:16:16,768
RIGHT OUT OF THE BOTTLE.

401
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:21,564
JOEY.

402
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:23,149
ROSS.

403
00:16:24,859 --> 00:16:26,903
BEN.

404
00:16:26,903 --> 00:16:28,863
I MEAN, BEN, BEN.

405
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:30,197
OKAY. 

406
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:31,825
RAYMOND, JOEY,
YOU'RE UP.

407
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:36,454
HEY.

408
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:37,956
OKAY.

409
00:16:37,956 --> 00:16:39,998
ALL RIGHT. WELL, LET'S...
LET'S TRY ONE.

410
00:16:39,998 --> 00:16:41,459
WHENEVER YOU GUYS ARE READY.

411
00:16:42,669 --> 00:16:43,795
UH-OH.

412
00:16:43,795 --> 00:16:45,045
IS THERE A PROBLEM?

413
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,631
WELL, THIS IS NOODLE SOUP

414
00:16:46,631 --> 00:16:48,758
AND I'VE BEEN
WORKING WITH TOMATO.

415
00:16:48,758 --> 00:16:50,217
SO... BUT THAT'S OKAY.

416
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:51,719
NO PROBLEM, NO PROBLEM.

417
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:52,929
MMM, NOODLE SOUP.

418
00:16:52,929 --> 00:16:54,096
YEAH.

419
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,181
YOU KNOW, THAT-THAT'S FINE

420
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:57,600
BUT THE LINE IS, "MMM, SOUP."

421
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,017
OH. WHAT DID I SAY?

422
00:16:59,017 --> 00:17:00,687
"MMM, NOODLE SOUP."

423
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,064
HOW'S THAT DIFFERENT?

424
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:10,488
OH! I SEE, YEAH.

425
00:17:10,488 --> 00:17:11,531
ALL RIGHT?

426
00:17:11,531 --> 00:17:13,073
LET'S TRY ONE.

427
00:17:16,577 --> 00:17:20,289
MMM, NOODLE SOUP.

428
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:23,877
OKAY.

429
00:17:23,877 --> 00:17:25,127
LET'S... TRY IT AGAIN.

430
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:26,295
OKAY.

431
00:17:28,882 --> 00:17:31,551
MMM, SOUP.

432
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:32,719
I MEAN NOODLE SOUP.

433
00:17:32,719 --> 00:17:33,720
I MEAN SOUP.

434
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:34,804
COME ON!

435
00:17:37,932 --> 00:17:39,893
YOU KNOW WHAT?
WE NEED TO MOVE ON.

436
00:17:39,893 --> 00:17:42,186
NO, I COULD DO IT ONE MORE TIME.
SEE, LOOK.

437
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:45,857
MMM, NOODLE SOUP.

438
00:17:45,857 --> 00:17:47,441
DAMN IT!

439
00:17:56,951 --> 00:17:58,953
HEY. HEY!

440
00:17:58,953 --> 00:18:01,497
UH-OH. BUSTED.

441
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:02,957
WELL, COME ON, YOU GUYS.

442
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:04,291
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

443
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,335
I THOUGHT WE WERE
THE PATCH SISTERS.

444
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,046
YEAH. THAT
DIDN'T WORK OUT.

445
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,550
RACHEL, WE TRIED TO QUIT,
BUT IT WAS TOO HARD.

446
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:14,510
WELL, YOU KNOW,
IF YOU STARTED SMOKING AGAIN

447
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,095
YOU COULD HAVE AT LEAST TOLD ME.

448
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:18,848
COME ON. GIVE ME ONE OF THOSE.
WHAT ARE WE TALKING ABOUT?

449
00:18:18,848 --> 00:18:20,224
NO, NO. YOU'RE DOING GREAT.
DON'T YOU GIVE UP.

450
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:21,935
THAT'S WHY WE
DIDN'T TELL YOU

451
00:18:21,935 --> 00:18:23,686
AND WE ARE NOT
GOING TO DRAG
YOU DOWN WITH US.

452
00:18:23,686 --> 00:18:25,730
WAIT. NO, NO,
NO. DRAG ME DOWN.
DRAG-DRAG ME DOWN.

453
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,440
FORGET IT, RACHEL.

454
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,733
WE'RE BOTH SO PROUD
OF HOW WELL YOU'RE DOING.

455
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:30,526
I'M NOT GOING
TO LET YOU BLOW IT.

456
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,653
IN FACT, IF I CATCH YOU
WITH A CIGARETTE, YOU'RE FIRED.

457
00:18:32,653 --> 00:18:35,114
GO ON. I DON'T WANT YOU
BREATHING THIS STUFF. GO ON.

458
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:37,199
ALL RIGHT.

459
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,744
SO YOU'LL COME WITH ME
ON THE PARIS TRIP?

460
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:41,328
OH, MAN!

461
00:18:44,999 --> 00:18:46,500
Chandler:
HEY.

462
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,002
HEY, CHECK IT OUT.

463
00:18:48,002 --> 00:18:50,713
UM, CUP HAT, CUP BANNER,
CUP CHANDELIER

464
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:52,048
AND THE THING THAT
STARTED IT ALL--

465
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:54,801
THE CUP.

466
00:18:54,801 --> 00:18:56,260
GREAT JOB
WITH THE CUPS, PHEEBS.

467
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:58,012
( giggling )

468
00:18:58,012 --> 00:19:02,308
WHY DON'T YOU JUST
GO OUT WITH HER?

469
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:03,643
AND DID YOU
NOTICE THE ICE?

470
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:04,978
LOOK, WE HAVE IT ALL--

471
00:19:04,978 --> 00:19:07,897
WE HAVE CRUSHED,
CUBED AND DRY.

472
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:08,898
WATCH.

473
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:11,901
AHH... MYSTICAL.

474
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:13,486
OH, YES.

475
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:16,656
CHANDLER...

476
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:17,949
IF IT WEREN'T...

477
00:19:17,949 --> 00:19:19,659
NO ONE'S EATING
MY TUSCAN FINGER FOOD

478
00:19:19,659 --> 00:19:21,243
BECAUSE THEY'RE ALL FILLING UP
ON PHOEBE'S SNO-CONES.

479
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:22,369
THERE ARE SNO-CONES?

480
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,414
SNO-CONES? YECH!

481
00:19:26,833 --> 00:19:27,959
YOU KNOW, GO, GO.
THANK YOU, THANK YOU.

482
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:31,754
Phoebe:
OH, LOOK, LOOK!

483
00:19:31,754 --> 00:19:34,340
All:
SURPRISE!

484
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,925
WHAT?!

485
00:19:35,925 --> 00:19:38,218
MY BIRTHDAY
IS NOT FOR ANOTHER MONTH.

486
00:19:38,218 --> 00:19:40,721
THAT'S THE SURPRISE.

487
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:42,222
OH, MY GOD.

488
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:44,391
YOU GUYS,
THIS IS SO GREAT.

489
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:46,393
IT'S SO UNEXPECTED.

490
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:49,939
I MEAN, CHANDLER'S BIRTHDAY'S
EVEN BEFORE MINE.

491
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:54,527
( weakly ):
SURPRISE.

492
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:59,615
WOW! THIS IS SO GREAT.

493
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:02,576
LOOK AT ALL THESE... CUPS.

494
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:04,745
THIS IS SO WEIRD.

495
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:07,123
I WAS IN CHARGE OF CUPS.

496
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:09,792
OH, OKAY. NOT SO WEIRD.

497
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:13,462
HEY.

498
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,589
HEY.

499
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:18,384
LISTEN, MAN, UH... I'M SORRY
THE AUDITION DIDN'T GO WELL.

500
00:20:18,384 --> 00:20:19,969
( snorts ):
YEAH, RIGHT.

501
00:20:19,969 --> 00:20:22,096
NO, REALLY, I AM, JOEY.

502
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:23,430
I FEEL BAD.

503
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:25,307
YEAH, WELL,
LOOK, ROSS...

504
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:27,101
YOU DON'T
HAVE TO, OKAY?

505
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:29,145
IT'S NOT YOUR FAULT I SUCK.

506
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:30,771
I MEAN, WHAT KIND OF ACTOR
CAN'T EVEN SAY,

507
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,606
"MMM! NOODLE SOUP"?

508
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:39,697
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT? MAYBE...
MAYBE YOU DIDN'T MESS UP

509
00:20:39,697 --> 00:20:42,825
YOUR AUDITION
BECAUSE YOU SUCK.

510
00:20:42,825 --> 00:20:47,788
MAYBE YOU MESSED UP
BECAUSE YOU CARE MORE
ABOUT YOUR GODSON.

511
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,082
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

512
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:51,584
I THINK
SUBCONSCIOUSLY...

513
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:54,128
WHOA-WHOA. YOU LOST ME.

514
00:20:57,381 --> 00:20:59,675
I THINK ON SOME LEVEL

515
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:03,054
YOU-YOU SABOTAGED
YOUR OWN AUDITION

516
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:05,806
SO BEN WOULD GET THE PART.

517
00:21:08,059 --> 00:21:11,896
WELL, YOUR WAY SOUNDS
A LOT BETTER THAN MINE.

518
00:21:11,896 --> 00:21:15,691
YEAH. YEAH. IT'S NOT THAT
I'M A BAD ACTOR...

519
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:18,027
NO.

520
00:21:18,027 --> 00:21:21,114
NO, IT'S JUST THAT, UH,
I CARE SO DAMN MUCH
ABOUT LITTLE BEN

521
00:21:21,114 --> 00:21:24,200
THAT, UH, IT WAS MORE
IMPORTANT FOR ME TO
SEE HIM SUCCEED.

522
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,451
THERE YOU GO.
YEAH.

523
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:26,911
THANK YOU.
THANK YOU.

524
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:28,996
SO, DID HE GET IT?
NO.

525
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,456
AH, WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

526
00:21:36,587 --> 00:21:38,965
IS RACHEL HERE?

527
00:21:38,965 --> 00:21:40,340
I'M MEETING HER
FOR LUNCH.

528
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,801
SHE DOESN'T COME DOWN HERE
ANYMORE.

529
00:21:41,801 --> 00:21:43,469
YOU CAN FIND HER UP ON TEN.

530
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:45,387
OKAY, GREAT.

531
00:21:58,192 --> 00:22:00,319
I'LL CATCH YOU GUYS LATER.

